                        explainText: 'This policy allows you to choose how to switch focus between windows.\n\nAvailable options:\n\nTriggered on click \u2014 windows become active when clicked;\n\nTriggered on hover \u2014 windows become active when the cursor moves over them. Hovering over the desktop does not change the activity;\n\nFocus follows mouse \u2014 windows become active when moved over them. Hovering over the desktop deactivates the previous window.\n\nThe "Raise window above others when focus is set" option is only effective if the focus mode is set to "Triggered on hover" or "Focus follows mouse".\n\nThe "Block" option (available only for the machine policy) prevents the user from changing the setting. Blocking a policy makes it take precedence over a similar policy for the user.',
