                    explainText: 'This policy allows you to disable the "net." prefix in the names of symbolic links to network drive mount directories\n\nWhen the "Map machine network drives in the home directory" policy is enabled, the symbolic link name is set as follows:\n\n~/net.{drives.system} \u2014 for system network drives and ~/.net.{drives.system} \u2014 for hidden system network drives.\n\nWhen the "Map user network drives in the home directory" policy is enabled, the symbolic link name is set as follows:\n\n~/net.{drives} \u2014 for user network drives and ~/.net.{drives} \u2014 for hidden user network drives.\n\nIf the policy is disabled or not configured, the names of symbolic links to mount directories begin with the prefix "net."\n\nThe "net." prefix is \u200B\u200Bremoved from the link names depending on the selected options.',
